    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0477" n="403" xml:id="pg403"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1351</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Moscow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Summers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-20T12:00:00+02:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 20, 1918, 12 noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received March 23, 9.55 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>278. The <hi rendition="#italic">Russkoe Slovo</hi> publishes following interview
                    with Trotsky regarding alliance of the
                    United States with the Soviet government: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Such an alliance is impossible. The Russia of the Soviets cannot align
                            itself by determinate engagements with capitalistic America, for this
                            would be a betrayal of its [omission]. It is possible that America is
                            seeking such a <hi rendition="#italic">rapprochement</hi> with us,
                            driven in so doing by its antagonism towards Japan, but in any case
                            there can be no question of an alliance by us of any nature with a <hi
                                rendition="#italic">bourgeois</hi> nation.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The Department can easily realize the danger of such statements to our present
                    friendly relations with Japan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
